      <section class="authority-panel" aria-labelledby="methodology-title">
        <h3 id="methodology-title">How this calculator works</h3>
        <p>
          The calculator applies Watt's law for DC and resistive loads, then
          adds power factor for AC loads and the 1.732 multiplier for balanced
          three-phase line-to-line calculations.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>DC and resistive loads: <strong>W = A x V</strong></li>
          <li>Single-phase AC: <strong>W = A x V x PF</strong></li>
          <li>Three-phase AC: <strong>W = 1.732 x A x V x PF</strong></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

